1. Give a clear, prepared description or presentation on general topics, with reasons in support of or against a particular point of view.

1. Give a clear, prepared description or presentation on general topics, with reasons in support of or against a particular point of view.

2. Initiate and maintain a conversation or related to everyday life.

3. Communicate spontaneously on general topics without grammatical errors that cause misunderstanding.

4. Understand videos and recorded audio material presenting every day conversations, documentaries or lectures on general topics, delivered in standard dialect.

5. Have responsibility and ethical awareness.

